I have a small problem using Stefan's exact.matches function.

When I introduce the following line:

matches.ficar<-exact.matches("\\bfic(a|á|o)(|s|r|mos|m|u|ste|ram)", sarptg, lines.around = 2)

The output generates tabs around  the first part of the regex only, as in:

sempre\tfica\tram longe

hospitais\tfica\tm

Is this a problem in the function itself or did I formulate my regex wrongly?

Thanks for your comments!

